虽然她早上刚开始时有点担心，对吧？

656
00:28:56.720 --> 00:28:57.780
Did Dwight make it?
德怀特成功了吗？

657
00:28:57.920 --> 00:28:59.180
Is everything going to be OK?
一切都会好吗？

658
00:29:00.420 --> 00:29:06.380
But she's a lady in love and her man has done this amazingly gallant thing for her.
但她现在是个坠入爱河的女人，她的男人为她做了这件极其英勇的事。

659
00:29:06.620 --> 00:29:10.820
And I feel like she's sort of dressing the part of like this lady in love.
我觉得她有点像是在打扮成那种坠入爱河的淑女。

660
00:29:10.940 --> 00:29:15.880
She's wearing her Janet Jackson Rhythm Nation mini short sleeve jacket.
她穿上了她那件珍妮·杰克逊《Rhythm Nation》风格的迷你短袖夹克。

661
00:29:15.880 --> 00:29:17.460
That's made a callback.
那是一个致敬梗。

662
00:29:18.320 --> 00:29:21.700
And she did a little something extra fancy with her hair.
而且她在发型上也做了一些额外精致的处理。

663
00:29:22.020 --> 00:29:25.100
Kim and I just thought maybe she's just she's taking it up a notch.
金和我只是觉得，也许她想把造型提升一个档次。

664
00:29:25.720 --> 00:29:26.100
Yeah.
没错。

665
00:29:26.380 --> 00:29:29.480
She turned her hair into a pinwheel flower.
她把头发盘成了一朵风车花。

666
00:29:29.640 --> 00:29:33.000
And clearly she has eight arms and multiple mirrors.
显然她得有八只手和好几面镜子才行。

667
00:29:33.180 --> 00:29:35.500
Because how do you do that to the back of your head?
因为你怎么可能把后脑勺弄成那样？

668
00:29:35.680 --> 00:29:39.580
Well, when I saw that hair, all I could think about was, oh, my gosh,
嗯，当我看到那个发型时，我满脑子想的都是，天哪，

669
00:29:39.580 --> 00:29:45.380
she couldn't lay down during her breaks because sometimes at lunch I would want to,
她在休息时肯定没法躺下，因为有时候午饭后我想，

670
00:29:45.520 --> 00:29:51.400
you know, lay back after I eat, maybe snooze it out because we would get up real early.
你知道，吃完饭后想往后靠一靠，或者小睡一会儿，因为我们起得很早。

671
00:29:51.860 --> 00:29:53.600
Sometimes I need a little snooze at lunch.
有时候我午饭时需要小睡一下。

672
00:29:53.760 --> 00:29:57.020
But you you couldn't do that that week, I guess.
但我想那一周你肯定做不到。

673
00:29:57.540 --> 00:29:58.380
Couldn't lay on that.
没法躺在上面。

674
00:29:58.480 --> 00:29:59.320
That would be so uncomfortable.
那会非常不舒服。

675
00:29:59.760 --> 00:30:02.080
I couldn't even lean back on a chair, lady.
我甚至连靠在椅子上都做不到，女士。

676
00:30:02.660 --> 00:30:05.520
I couldn't even recline in any way.
我甚至没法以任何方式后仰。

677
00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:07.080
Guys, check it out.
伙计们，看看这个。

678
00:30:07.180 --> 00:30:08.180
You don't have to look hard.
你们不用费劲就能看到。

679
00:30:08.180 --> 00:30:08.920
It's insane.
太疯狂了。

680
00:30:09.200 --> 00:30:10.400
It's also amazing.
但也太惊人了。

681
00:30:10.800 --> 00:30:12.800
We had a lot of people write in.
我们收到了很多人的来信。

682
00:30:12.980 --> 00:30:17.460
Julia Lee, Bethany Devish, Kaylee Waiting, Anita Prasad.
朱莉娅·李、贝瑟尼·德维什、凯莉·韦廷、安妮塔·普拉萨德。

683
00:30:18.080 --> 00:30:22.340
They all said Angela's hair looks incredible in this episode.
她们都说安吉拉在这一集里的发型看起来棒极了。

684
00:30:22.940 --> 00:30:23.900
Thank you.
谢谢。

685
00:30:24.140 --> 00:30:25.420
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

686
00:30:25.720 --> 00:30:30.180
And now we're going to come up onto this talking head that Rashida actually mentioned
现在我们要聊到拉什达在做客《Benihana》那一集时提到的采访片段，

687
00:30:30.180 --> 00:30:35.460
when she was a guest on Benihana, where Andy talks about him and Karen being the last
安迪在里面说他和凯伦是最后

688
00:30:35.460 --> 00:30:37.140
two left standing, right?
剩下的两个人，对吧？

689
00:30:38.080 --> 00:30:42.440
And Andy says he's not going to be one of the kids touring Willy Wonka's factory.
安迪说他不会成为参观威利·旺卡工厂的孩子之一。

690
00:30:42.680 --> 00:30:44.640
He will not fall into the chocolate river.
他不会掉进巧克力河里。

691
00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:46.440
I loved that reference.
我很喜欢那个梗。

692
00:30:46.780 --> 00:30:47.700
I loved it too.
我也很喜欢。

693
00:30:47.700 --> 00:30:52.720
But all I could think about, Jenna, is that he does fall into the lake.
但珍娜，我满脑子想的都是，他确实掉进湖里了。

694
00:30:53.140 --> 00:30:53.700
When?
什么时候？

695
00:30:53.700 --> 00:30:55.380
At Beach Games.
在《海滩游戏》那一集。

696
00:30:55.680 --> 00:30:56.660
Totally forgot that.
完全忘了那回事了。

697
00:30:57.300 --> 00:30:58.920
He falls into the lake.
他掉进了湖里。

698
00:30:59.060 --> 00:31:02.180
He's in a giant sumo suit and he floats on by.
他穿着巨大的相扑服，然后漂走了。

699
00:31:02.440 --> 00:31:09.480
And I couldn't help but think what an amazing, like, callback to the Willy Wonka River thing.
我不禁想到，这和威利·旺卡的河流梗呼应得真是太妙了。

700
00:31:09.640 --> 00:31:10.100
I don't know.
我不知道。

701
00:31:10.200 --> 00:31:11.100
I thought that was kind of fun.
我觉得那挺有意思的。

702
00:31:11.280 --> 00:31:12.020
Oh, my God.
天哪。

703
00:31:12.020 --> 00:31:12.440
Yeah.
是啊。

704
00:31:12.780 --> 00:31:13.340
I totally.
我完全同意。

705
00:31:13.520 --> 00:31:13.840
Yes.
没错。

706
00:31:13.960 --> 00:31:14.740
I'm so sorry.
真抱歉。

707
00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:16.580
It's all coming back to me.
我全都想起来了。

708
00:31:17.120 --> 00:31:19.160
We'll get to it when we talk about Beach Games.
等我们聊到“海滩游戏”那一集时再说吧。

709
00:31:19.160 --> 00:31:21.380
But, yes, Ed's slowly floating away.
不过，没错，埃德正在慢慢飘走。

710
00:31:21.420 --> 00:31:23.320
I remember it now so clearly.
我现在记得清清楚楚。

711
00:31:23.800 --> 00:31:26.980
So, Angela, now you're standing at reception.
那么，安吉拉，现在你站在前台。

712
00:31:27.360 --> 00:31:29.600
You're getting yourself some jelly beans.
你正在拿些软糖吃。

713
00:31:29.700 --> 00:31:31.340
And Dwight comes in.
然后德怀特进来了。

714
00:31:31.780 --> 00:31:33.100
It's so sweet.
太甜了。

715
00:31:33.100 --> 00:31:36.900
He lets you know the tax forms have been delivered.
他告诉你税务表格已经送到了。

716
00:31:37.580 --> 00:31:38.040
Yes.
是的。

717
00:31:38.040 --> 00:31:42.440
You guys are kind of talking in code, but, of course, Pam is clocking it all.
你们俩像是在用暗语交流，但当然，帕姆把这一切都看在眼里。

718
00:31:42.640 --> 00:31:48.580
And then as you walk away, you say, I don't want these, and you leave the jelly beans.
然后当你走开时，你说：“我不想要这些”，就把软糖留下了。

719
00:31:49.600 --> 00:31:50.960
We had a fan question.
我们有个粉丝提问。

720
00:31:51.680 --> 00:31:51.900
Okay.
好的。

721
00:31:52.260 --> 00:32:00.460
Allie Jo Higginbotham says, did Angela improv that line, I don't want these, to Pam, after she took the jelly beans?
艾莉·乔·希金博瑟姆问，安吉拉在拿了软糖之后，对帕姆说的那句“我不想要这些”，是即兴发挥的吗？

722
00:32:01.540 --> 00:32:02.060
Yes.
是的。

723
00:32:02.580 --> 00:32:03.640
Yes, I did.
没错，是我即兴说的。

724
00:32:04.400 --> 00:32:11.320
The note that Greg had given me in that scene is that, you know, I'm so anxious to talk to Dwight to find out that everything went okay.
格雷格在那场戏里给我的指示是，你知道，我当时急着想和德怀特说话，确认一切是否顺利。

725
00:32:11.320 --> 00:32:13.880
But I had to make some business for myself.
但我得给自己找点事做。

726
00:32:14.020 --> 00:32:15.260
Like, why would I be at reception?
比如，我为什么会站在前台？

727
00:32:15.680 --> 00:32:18.180
So, I decided to kind of dig in the jelly beans.
所以我决定去翻翻那些软糖。

728
00:32:18.340 --> 00:32:20.420
I just sort of was like, oh, this is what I'll do.
我当时就是觉得，哦，我就这么做吧。

729
00:32:20.940 --> 00:32:24.680
So, I was digging in the jelly beans, and I put a few in my hand throughout the scene.
于是我就在那翻软糖，在整场戏里手里抓了几颗。

730
00:32:25.100 --> 00:32:27.660
And then as Dwight walked away, I just had them in my hand.
然后当德怀特走开时，我手里还抓着它们。

731
00:32:27.660 --> 00:32:31.280
So, I just placed them on the countertop, like your kid would.
所以我就像小孩子一样，把它们放在了柜台上。

732
00:32:31.420 --> 00:32:32.260
I don't like this.
我不喜欢这个。

733
00:32:32.680 --> 00:32:32.960
Yes.
没错。

734
00:32:32.960 --> 00:32:33.940
And just walked away.
然后就走开了。

735
00:32:34.260 --> 00:32:36.720
And it just tickled us so much.
这把我们逗乐坏了。

736
00:32:36.720 --> 00:32:37.880
And they left it in.
他们还把这一幕留在了正片里。

737
00:32:38.020 --> 00:32:42.360
But the part I love even more, Jenna, is your look.
但珍娜，我更喜欢的是你的表情。

738
00:32:42.620 --> 00:32:47.140
Your look of like, it said so much to me in the moment.
你当时那种表情，在那一刻对我来说意味深长。

739
00:32:47.300 --> 00:32:52.720
It said people leave their water bottles and their trash on my desk.
那表情仿佛在说，人们总是把水瓶和垃圾留在我的桌子上。

740
00:32:53.080 --> 00:32:53.900
All the time.
一直都是这样。

741
00:32:54.120 --> 00:32:58.300
After you would leave the jelly beans, I added a little bit that got cut out.
在你留下软糖之后，我还加了一小段戏，不过被剪掉了。

742
00:32:58.440 --> 00:33:01.340
And probably it should have been cut out because it just would have gone on forever.
可能确实应该剪掉，因为如果不剪的话，那段戏就没完没了了。

743
00:33:01.340 --> 00:33:05.920
But I would find all these various ways to get rid of the jelly beans.
我当时想出了各种各样处理这些软糖的方法。

744
00:33:05.920 --> 00:33:11.480
So, I remember one time I picked up the trash can and I scooched them into the trash can using a piece of paper.
我记得有一次我拿起垃圾桶，用一张纸把它们扫进了垃圾桶里。

745
00:33:11.700 --> 00:33:16.560
And another time I, like, took a tissue and I picked them up with a tissue.
还有一次，我拿了张纸巾，用纸巾把它们捡了起来。

746
00:33:17.560 --> 00:33:21.760
And another time I think I picked them up and put them back in the jelly bean container.
还有一次我想我是把它们捡起来，放回了软糖罐子里。

747
00:33:21.760 --> 00:33:27.180
But I had, I know, I had all these ways that I got rid of these jelly beans.
我知道，我当时想出了各种处理这些软糖的方法。

748
00:33:27.400 --> 00:33:29.160
And I had a good time with that.
我玩得很开心。

749
00:33:29.360 --> 00:33:30.660
None of them made it in, of course.
当然，这些都没被剪进正片里。

750
00:33:30.880 --> 00:33:34.240
But it was just kind of like a fun little bit we were doing.
但这只是我们当时做的一个有趣的小片段。

751
00:33:34.540 --> 00:33:37.280
So, should we move into the conference room now, Angela?
那么，安吉拉，我们现在要进会议室吗？

752
00:33:37.280 --> 00:33:41.820
Oh, yeah, because somebody needs to pass the tarty sauce.
哦，是啊，因为总得有人去递塔塔酱。

753
00:33:42.240 --> 00:33:42.660
Yes.
是的。

754
00:33:42.900 --> 00:33:47.300
The entire sales team is assembled in the conference room and Dwight comes in late.
整个销售团队都在会议室集合了，德怀特迟到了。

755
00:33:47.480 --> 00:33:49.620
So, Andy is such a tool.
安迪真是个十足的蠢货。

756
00:33:49.820 --> 00:33:50.780
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

757
00:33:51.040 --> 00:33:56.480
So, at the beginning of this scene, Michael explains that this is his dream team.
在这个场景开始时，迈克尔解释说这是他的梦之队。

758
00:33:56.480 --> 00:33:58.500
This is my dream sales team.
这是我的梦之销售团队。

759
00:33:58.500 --> 00:34:01.140
And we're going to pair up and go on some sales calls.
我们要两两分组，去进行一些销售拜访。

760
00:34:01.140 --> 00:34:05.020
And we had a fan question from Holly Ennarson.
我们收到了粉丝霍莉·恩纳森的一个提问。

761
00:34:05.600 --> 00:34:07.500
Holly Ennarson says,
霍莉·恩纳森说，

762
00:34:08.100 --> 00:34:11.880
Phyllis blows her nose right after Michael says,
菲利斯在迈克尔说完这句话后立刻擤了鼻涕，

763
00:34:12.080 --> 00:34:13.860
This is my dream team.
这是我的梦之队。

764
00:34:13.980 --> 00:34:15.860
Was that scripted?
那是剧本里写的吗？

765
00:34:16.020 --> 00:34:18.780
I wondered the same thing because it's brilliant.
我也在想同样的问题，因为那太精彩了。

766
00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:20.640
The timing is so perfect.
时机把握得太完美了。

767
00:34:21.060 --> 00:34:22.320
It's so perfect.
简直太完美了。

768
00:34:23.020 --> 00:34:24.900
Yes, it was scripted.
是的，那是剧本里写的。

769
00:34:25.040 --> 00:34:25.520
Amazing.
太棒了。

770
00:34:26.020 --> 00:34:27.840
Here is the script direction.
这是剧本里的指示。

771
00:34:28.340 --> 00:34:29.040
Quote,
引用如下：

772
00:34:29.040 --> 00:34:32.720
The camera pans to bored faces of the sales team.
镜头扫过销售团队一张张无聊的脸。

773
00:34:33.100 --> 00:34:34.680
Phyllis blows her nose.
菲利斯擤了擤鼻涕。

774
00:34:36.960 --> 00:34:41.900
And, you know, guys, this is a little moment because I watched it several times.
而且，伙计们，这是一个小细节，因为我看了好几遍。

775
00:34:42.880 --> 00:34:44.060
It's so great.
太棒了。

776
00:34:44.560 --> 00:34:46.240
Phyllis gets out her little tissue.
菲利斯拿出了她的小纸巾。

777
00:34:46.480 --> 00:34:48.280
She sniffles a little bit.
她吸了吸鼻子。

778
00:34:48.460 --> 00:34:50.000
And then she blows her nose.
然后她擤了鼻涕。

779
00:34:50.360 --> 00:34:52.520
Like, she times it perfectly.
她掐的时间点太准了。

780
00:34:52.520 --> 00:34:54.980
But she starts the bit a little early.
但她开始得稍微早了一点。

781
00:34:55.780 --> 00:34:58.820
And I think that's what sells making it look so organic.
我觉得正是这一点让它看起来如此自然。

782
00:34:59.040 --> 00:35:01.220
It's really wonderful work.
这真是非常精彩的表演。

783
00:35:01.360 --> 00:35:02.380
Little details.
小细节。

784
00:35:02.640 --> 00:35:04.940
Phyllis, man, with the tissue work.
菲利斯，天哪，那纸巾用得太绝了。

785
00:35:05.100 --> 00:35:06.880
So everyone gets paired up.
大家都分好了组。

786
00:35:07.080 --> 00:35:15.340
Yes, we get Karen and Phyllis and Ryan and Stanley, Dwight and Jim and Michael and Andy.
是的，凯伦和菲利斯，瑞安和斯坦利，德怀特和吉姆，迈克尔和安迪。

787
00:35:15.560 --> 00:35:19.100
Now they're going to go out and be in cars together all day.
现在他们要一起开车出去，整天待在一起。

788
00:35:19.100 --> 00:35:20.080
I couldn't wait.
我简直等不及了。

789
00:35:20.080 --> 00:35:22.560
I remember when we got the script, Jenna, at the table read.
珍娜，我记得我们拿到剧本在围读的时候。

790
00:35:22.700 --> 00:35:26.680
When I saw, like, the groupings, I was like, oh, this is going to be so fun.
当我看到分组时，我就想，哦，这一定会很有趣。

791
00:35:27.100 --> 00:35:31.560
Well, there's a Ryan talking head in here that makes me laugh so hard.
对了，这里有个瑞安的单人采访片段，让我笑得不行。

792
00:35:31.860 --> 00:35:33.940
Because you are now Ryan in real life.
因为你现在在现实生活中就是瑞安。

793
00:35:33.980 --> 00:35:34.940
I am now Ryan.
我现在就是瑞安。

794
00:35:34.940 --> 00:35:40.700
I love it that he said he's flattered to be Stanley's second choice after pass.
我喜欢他说自己很荣幸成为斯坦利在“放弃”之后的第二选择。

795
00:35:42.320 --> 00:35:43.280
After pass.
在“放弃”之后。

796
00:35:43.920 --> 00:35:45.380
Stanley got to pick his partner.
斯坦利可以挑选他的搭档。

797
00:35:45.600 --> 00:35:47.600
And his first response was pass.
他的第一反应是放弃。

798
00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:51.160
And his second response was, I guess he'll take the kid.
而他的第二反应是，我想他只能选那个孩子了。

799
00:35:51.720 --> 00:35:55.300
Well, I wanted to talk really quickly about Jim's talking head.
对了，我想快速聊聊吉姆的那个单人采访片段。

800
00:35:55.520 --> 00:35:59.380
He holds up that photo of Dwight and Jim, like the old photo.
他举起了那张德怀特和吉姆的照片，就是那张旧照片。

801
00:35:59.560 --> 00:36:04.200
Because they clearly have been on a ton of sales calls together, right?
因为他们显然一起打过无数次销售电话，对吧？

802
00:36:04.300 --> 00:36:07.480
And it shows their history a little bit, which I love.
这多少体现了他们的过往，我喜欢这一点。

803
00:36:07.640 --> 00:36:14.400
But in the DVD commentary, Rain said that his hair in that photo was from 1991.
但在DVD评论音轨里，雷恩说那张照片里他的发型是1991年的。

804
00:36:14.700 --> 00:36:18.620
He was on tour with an acting company doing Romeo and Juliet.
当时他正随一个剧团巡演《罗密欧与朱丽叶》。

805
00:36:18.620 --> 00:36:21.400
And they all had long Elizabethan hair.
